@startuml PropORACLE_Payout_Scrape
' Payout capture — PrizePicks N-correct via CDP; a scheduled publisher in its own right
' Render: PlantUML extension or https://www.plantuml.com/plantuml

title PropORACLE — Payout scrape (N-correct only)

start
:Task Scheduler window\n(D-1 9PM · 1AM · 5AM · 8AM · 9 ·\n9:45 · 10:30 · 1PM · 4:30)\nor manual -UpdateOnly;

if (Dual card exists for slate D?\n(Goblin-70 + mixer --write-web)) then (no)
  :Skip — nothing to price;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

if (Single-flight lock free?) then (no)
  :Skip this window;
  stop
else (yes)
endif

if (Chrome :9222 up?) then (no)
  :Skip CDP;
  :Display keeps last floor\n(VERIFY: fitted payout_rate_card.json\nwith non-live payout_source);
  stop
else (yes)
endif

if (First scrape of slate D?\n(D-1 9PM, -Force)) then (yes)
  :CDP scrape **all** generated slips;
else (no)
  if (missing live_cdp OR line/type moved?) then (yes)
    :Re-scrape those slips only;
    note right
      Current scrub drops **whole** tickets
      (no shrink), so leg-count / live_cdp
      clear is not required for that path.
      Remaining risk is the **lock race**:
      capture without scrub under the same
      payout_capture.lock can rewrite a
      just-scrubbed card (see ticket-design).
    end note
  else (no)
    :Skip CDP;
    stop
  endif
endif

:Chrome :9222 → PrizePicks slip;
:Read **N-correct pays Xx**\n(Power: N-correct ·\nFlex N: N-correct and N−1-correct);
note right
  NEVER store the 1st-place multiplier.
end note

:payout_patch_<date>.json;
:Write back display_min_x\npayout_source = live_cdp;
:Publish-LiveSite.ps1 → origin/main;
stop

floating note right
  scripts/run_live_payout_capture.ps1
  -Force      = full dual-card re-scrape
  -UpdateOnly = incremental (manual / CDP-down recovery)
  Publishes on its own schedule — not only as a
  step under the dual-card build.
end note

@enduml
